    "correct_answer": "A",
    "solution_latex": "In planes at angle $\\alpha$ and $90^\\circ - \\alpha$ to magnetic meridian, horizontal components are $B_H\\cos\\alpha$ and $B_H\\sin\\alpha$. Apparent dips give $\\tan\\delta_1 = \\frac{B_V}{B_H\\cos\\alpha}$ and $\\tan\\delta_2 = \\frac{B_V}{B_H\\sin\\alpha}$. Inverting gives $\\cot\\delta_1 = \\cot\\delta\\cos\\alpha$ and $\\cot\\delta_2 = \\cot\\delta\\sin\\alpha$. Squaring and adding: $\\cot^2\\delta_1 + \\cot^2\\delta_2 = \\cot^2\\delta(\\cos^2\\alpha + \\sin^2\\alpha) = \\cot^2\\delta$.",
