    "correct_answer_latex": "$\\mu_0 n_1 n_2 \\pi r_1^2$",
    "correct_answer": "A",
    "solution_latex": "Current $I_2$ in outer solenoid produces uniform interior field $B_2 = \\mu_0 n_2 I_2$. Flux linked with inner solenoid of cross-sectional area $\\pi r_1^2$ per unit length is $\\Phi_1 = n_1 (B_2 \\pi r_1^2) = \\mu_0 n_1 n_2 \\pi r_1^2 I_2$. Hence $M/l = \\mu_0 n_1 n_2 \\pi r_1^2$.",
    "socratic_hints": [
      "Inner solenoid has smaller area $\\pi r_1^2$.",
      "Flux through inner solenoid is $B_{\\text{outer}} \\times (\\pi r_1^2)$.",
      "Divide by $I$ to get $\\mu_0 n_1 n_2 \\pi r_1^2$."
    ],
