    "correct_answer_latex": "$P = \\frac{I}{c}$",
    "correct_answer": "A",
    "solution_latex": "Momentum transported by wave of energy $U$ is $p = U/c$. When light is completely absorbed, momentum transferred is $\\Delta p = p = U/c$. Radiation pressure is force per unit area: $P = \\frac{F}{A} = \\frac{\\Delta p / \\Delta t}{A} = \\frac{(U/\\Delta t)/A}{c} = \\frac{I}{c}$.",
